# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession draft Tailoring --out` from tools/lib/professions/routes/tailoring.json and data/forever. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/tailoring
title Tailoring 1-300
category Professions
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Tailoring weaves cloth into bolts, then sews the bolts into cloth armour and bags. Cloth drops
# from humanoids, so it needs no gathering profession; Enchanting suits it, as the green pieces it
# makes break into enchanting materials.
#
# Ranks: Apprentice at any level from any Tailoring trainer (the first trainer teaches recipes only
# up to 55); Journeyman from level 10 at the city trainers; Expert from level 20 (50s) at Georgio
# Bolero in Stormwind or Josef Gregorian in Undercity; Artisan from level 35 at Timothy Worthington
# on Theramore Isle or Daryl Stack in Tarren Mill.
#
# Two patterns come from vendors: Runecloth Gloves (Qia in Everlook) and Runecloth Cuffs (Pexmit in
# Mount Hyjal). Past 280 only world-drop patterns from the Auction House reach 300: Runecloth
# Shoulders or Wizardweave Turban. The Loom patterns from Silithus would also do, but no town has a
# Loom.
#
# The route (crafts are about what it takes; yellow and green recipes can take a few more):
# Apprentice (1-55), from level 1:
#    1-30  30 Bolt of Linen Cloth: 60 Linen Cloth
#   30-55  28 Linen Belt: 28 Coarse Thread, 28 Bolt of Linen Cloth
# Journeyman (55-140), from level 10:
#   55-80  37 Bolt of Woolen Cloth: 111 Wool Cloth
#   80-95  22 Woolen Cape: 22 Fine Thread, 22 Bolt of Woolen Cloth
#   95-100 5 Double-stitched Woolen Shoulders: 10 Fine Thread, 15 Bolt of Woolen Cloth
#  100-120 55 Bolt of Silk Cloth: 220 Silk Cloth
#  120-125 5 Azure Silk Hood: 5 Fine Thread, 10 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 10 Blue Dye
#  125-140 15 Small Silk Pack: 45 Fine Thread, 30 Heavy Leather, 45 Bolt of Silk Cloth
# Expert (140-200), from level 20:
#  140-150 23 Bolt of Mageweave: 115 Mageweave Cloth
#  make 80 Bolt of Silk Cloth: 320 Silk Cloth
#  150-170 20 Crimson Silk Vest: 40 Fine Thread, 40 Red Dye, 80 Bolt of Silk Cloth
#  make 68 Bolt of Silk Cloth: 272 Silk Cloth
#  170-185 17 Crimson Silk Pantaloons: 34 Red Dye, 34 Silken Thread, 68 Bolt of Silk Cloth
#  make 21 Bolt of Mageweave: 105 Mageweave Cloth
#  185-200 22 Black Mageweave Leggings: 66 Silken Thread, 44 Bolt of Mageweave
# Artisan (200-300), from level 35:
#  make 15 Bolt of Mageweave: 75 Mageweave Cloth
#  200-205 5 Black Mageweave Shoulders: 15 Bolt of Mageweave, 10 Heavy Silken Thread
#  205-215 23 Bolt of Runecloth: 115 Runecloth
#  make 68 Bolt of Mageweave: 340 Mageweave Cloth
#  215-225 17 Red Mageweave Bag: 34 Red Dye, 68 Bolt of Mageweave, 34 Heavy Silken Thread
#  make 49 Bolt of Runecloth: 245 Runecloth
#  225-240 24 Runecloth Belt: 72 Bolt of Runecloth, 24 Rune Thread
#  make 44 Bolt of Runecloth: 220 Runecloth
#  240-250 11 Runecloth Gloves: 44 Rugged Leather, 44 Bolt of Runecloth, 11 Rune Thread
#  make 195 Bolt of Runecloth: 975 Runecloth
#  250-280 39 Runecloth Cuffs: 195 Bolt of Runecloth, 39 Ironweb Spider Silk, 39 Rune Thread
#   with Pattern: Runecloth Shoulders:
#    make 406 Bolt of Runecloth: 2030 Runecloth
#    280-300 58 Runecloth Shoulders: 232 Rugged Leather, 406 Bolt of Runecloth, 116 Ironweb Spider Silk, 58 Rune Thread
#   with Pattern: Wizardweave Turban:
#    make 348 Bolt of Runecloth: 1740 Runecloth
#    280-300 58 Wizardweave Turban: 58 Star Ruby, 232 Dream Dust, 348 Bolt of Runecloth, 58 Rune Thread
#   Runecloth Cuffs (no plans):
#    make 155 Bolt of Runecloth: 775 Runecloth
#    280-290 31 Runecloth Cuffs: 155 Bolt of Runecloth, 31 Ironweb Spider Silk, 31 Rune Thread

section Tailoring 1-30

step Learn Tailoring
  tip No character level needed.
  train Tailoring Apprentice

step Buy 28 Coarse Thread
  tip For 28 Linen Belts.
